            ctx.sleep(180);
        }
        if ctx.should_exit() { return false; }
    }
    // need to account for PLAY/instant? PLAY and TASK also count as lines for instant? Original instant counts lines. Our sleep handling for PLAY/TASK used ctx.sleep which already handles instant. But we manually decremented for hosts. For PLAY/TASK we used sleep which handles instant. Good. But hosts we manually handled instant + sleep. Actually we did instant check manually, but also need to not double? We did: if instant_left>0 decrement else sleep. That's same as ctx.sleep but without the initial check? Good.
    // For simplicity, return true (completed). But ansible in original continues? Actually ansible module after hosts finishes? It just ends (no more output). So return true.
    true
}

